nst them, and playing a game of cat and mouse might be far more interesting. Especially if he's more interested in seeing if they deserve to die or wokring against true evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely, though I do wonder what you think of my concept a fictionalized/reimagined Gary where they tried to offset the decline of steel with kitschy tourism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T19:10:30-08:00","id":1529484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529482#post1529482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree completely, though I do wonder what you think of my concept a fictionalized/reimagined Gary where they tried to offset the decline of steel with kitschy tourism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It happened in real life.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine was driving to Chicago from Gary and asked where Gary ended.<br /> <br /> &quot;When the strip clubs and gambling joints end.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T20:52:28-08:00","id":1529487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529484#post1529484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It happened in real life.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine was driving to Chicago from Gary and asked where Gary ended.<br /> <br /> &quot;When the strip clubs and gambling joints end.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the things that inspired me, though that happened long after the city had essentially died.<br /> <br /> The strip clubs and casinos alongside the highway in modern Gary combined with kitschy tourist towns in New Jersey and in the South are part of what inspired this idea.<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think of my &quot;Canonical Order&quot; for Chicago 1E?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-26-2024, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T15:52:10-08:00","id":1529525,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the double-post, but I'm thinking I should create a &quot;Vampire 1E General Discussion&quot; thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T22:08:49-08:00","id":1529534,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's much difference between 1e and early 2e. There are only some minor game mechanical changes, and the setting is clearly the same. I think the real &quot;edition&quot; differences in pre-Revised Vampire is between the era of Andrew Greenberg (1991-1994) as Developer and post-Greenberg development (1995-1997). That second half of VtM 2e saw some reaction to some features people associated with the Greenberg era - fishmalks, vampions, and the controversy over Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand - as well as incorporation of new canon being created in the Vampire: the Dark Ages spinoff. It didn't result in continuity changes like what Revised did, but there was a shift in some tone, an increasing emphasis on battles between vampire sects rather than exploration of the world by newly made vampires, and increasing pushback by the gameline against &quot;wrongfun&quot; and trying to correct things they saw certain players doing which they thought clashed with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T04:53:48-08:00","id":1529543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529534#post1529534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's much difference between 1e and early 2e. There are only some minor game mechanical changes, and the setting is clearly the same. I think the real &quot;edition&quot; differences in pre-Revised Vampire is between the era of Andrew Greenberg (1991-1994) as Developer and post-Greenberg development (1995-1997). That second half of VtM 2e saw some reaction to some features people associated with the Greenberg era - fishmalks, vampions, and the controversy over Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand - as well as incorporation of new canon being created in the Vampire: the Dark Ages spinoff. It didn't result in continuity changes like what Revised did, but there was a shift in some tone, an increasing emphasis on battles between vampire sects rather than exploration of the world by newly made vampires, and increasing pushback by the gameline against &quot;wrongfun&quot; and trying to correct things they saw certain players doing which they thought clashed with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unironically, the Andrew Greenberg era was the greatest era for VTM, IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T05:10:33-08:00","id":1529544,"title":"","content":"I only started playing with V20, but I bought a few of the Greenberg-era products on DTRPG and in general I liked them very much (like I think I was one of the few people to actually like Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T07:44:54-08:00","id":1529550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529544#post1529544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only started playing with V20, but I bought a few of the Greenberg-era products on DTRPG and in general I liked them very much (like I think I was one of the few people to actually like Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you and me would get along very well at the gaming table<br /> <br /> Unironically, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand is a great book and gets way too much hate.<br /> <br /> At this point, most people nowadays just hate DSOTBH because certain later devs have been telling them to hate it for the past thirty years and folks on places like RPG.net, Reddit, and various other forums have been all too happy to reinforce the echo chamber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-27-2024, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T12:08:45-08:00","id":1529564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529534#post1529534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's much difference between 1e and early 2e. There are only some minor game mechanical changes, and the setting is clearly the same. I think the real &quot;edition&quot; differences in pre-Revised Vampire is between the era of Andrew Greenberg (1991-1994) as Developer and post-Greenberg development (1995-1997). That second half of VtM 2e saw some reaction to some features people associated with the Greenberg era - fishmalks, vampions, and the controversy over Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand - as well as incorporation of new canon being created in the Vampire: the Dark Ages spinoff. It didn't result in continuity changes like what Revised did, but there was a shift in some tone, an increasing emphasis on battles between vampire sects rather than exploration of the world by newly made vampires, and increasing pushback by the gameline against &quot;wrongfun&quot; and trying to correct things they saw certain players doing which they thought clashed with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly disagree and think there's a very strong difference between 1st Edition and 2nd Edition but that's not strictly a difference between Editions but more of a difference that has a Penumbra between them (to co-opt a werewolf term).<br /> <br /> In terms of THEME when people refer to 1st Edition, they mean the street level Chicago and street based Vampire: The Masquerade. Anarchs vs. Camarilla, Sabbat are mysterious inhuman monsters, Humanity focus, and Lupines as the only other defined supernatural. Players are meant to be Neonates and stick to one city.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic First Edition&quot;: Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, Blood Bond, Chicago by Night, Diablerie: Mexico, Hunter's Hunted, Milwaukee by Night, Mummy, The Succubus Club<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition moved the vampires to a more global non-American Midwest version. It defined the Sabbat as playable characters, introduced the Paths of Enlightenment as a chance to get away from Humanity, and also created a bunch of other new books. Berlin, Diablerie: Britain, Los Angeles, Vancouver, Montreal, and so on. Elders are introduced as an option by both Elysium and Dirty Secrets.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic Second Edition&quot;: The Player's Guide to the Sabbat, Children of the Inquisition, the Clan Books, Elysium, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, Kindeed of the East, and so son.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T12:10:19-08:00","id":1529565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529534#post1529534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's much difference between 1e and early 2e. There are only some minor game mechanical changes, and the setting is clearly the same. I think the real &quot;edition&quot; differences in pre-Revised Vampire is between the era of Andrew Greenberg (1991-1994) as Developer and post-Greenberg development (1995-1997). That second half of VtM 2e saw some reaction to some features people associated with the Greenberg era - fishmalks, vampions, and the controversy over Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand - as well as incorporation of new canon being created in the Vampire: the Dark Ages spinoff. It didn't result in continuity changes like what Revised did, but there was a shift in some tone, an increasing emphasis on battles between vampire sects rather than exploration of the world by newly made vampires, and increasing pushback by the gameline against &quot;wrongfun&quot; and trying to correct things they saw certain players doing which they thought clashed with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I think there's a very strong difference between 1st Edition and 2nd Edition but that's not strictly a difference between Editions but more of a difference that has a Penumbra between them (to co-opt a werewolf term).<br /> <br /> In terms of THEME when people refer to 1st Edition, they mean the street level Chicago and street based Vampire: The Masquerade. Anarchs vs. Camarilla, Sabbat are mysterious inhuman monsters, Humanity focus, and Lupines as the only other defined supernatural. Players are meant to be Neonates and stick to one city.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic First Edition&quot;: Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, Blood Bond, Chicago by Night, Diablerie: Mexico, Hunter's Hunted, Milwaukee by Night, Mummy, The Succubus Club<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition moved the vampires to a more global non-American Midwest version. It defined the Sabbat as playable characters, introduced the Paths of Enlightenment as a chance to get away from Humanity, and also created a bunch of other new books. Berlin, Diablerie: Britain, Los Angeles, Vancouver, Montreal, and so on. Elders are introduced as an option by both Elysium and Dirty Secrets.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic Second Edition&quot;: The Player's Guide to the Sabbat, Children of the Inquisition, the Clan Books, Elysium, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, Kindeed of the East, and so son.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T12:32:28-08:00","id":1529566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529565#post1529565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno. I think there's a very strong difference between 1st Edition and 2nd Edition but that's not strictly a difference between Editions but more of a difference that has a Penumbra between them (to co-opt a werewolf term).<br /> <br /> In terms of THEME when people refer to 1st Edition, they mean the street level Chicago and street based Vampire: The Masquerade. Anarchs vs. Camarilla, Sabbat are mysterious inhuman monsters, Humanity focus, and Lupines as the only other defined supernatural. Players are meant to be Neonates and stick to one city.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic First Edition&quot;: Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, Blood Bond, Chicago by Night, Diablerie: Mexico, Hunter's Hunted, Milwaukee by Night, Mummy, The Succubus Club<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition moved the vampires to a more global non-American Midwest version. It defined the Sabbat as playable characters, introduced the Paths of Enlightenment as a chance to get away from Humanity, and also created a bunch of other new books. Berlin, Diablerie: Britain, Los Angeles, Vancouver, Montreal, and so on. Elders are introduced as an option by both Elysium and Dirty Secrets.<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic Second Edition&quot;: The Player's Guide to the Sabbat, Children of the Inquisition, the Clan Books, Elysium, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, Kindeed of the East, and so son.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed to a point, though I will say that 1st Edition is far more &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas Vampions Badwrongfun&quot; than V5 and with no real metaplot to boot, and that's what makes it interesting to me. The fact that elements of the V5 crowd likes to present it as a &quot;return to form&quot; is utterly laughable. It's street-level but it's also more D&amp;D-like than the other editions of the game.<br /> <br /> Also, Lupines weren't the only other major supernatural force defined in 1e. You also had the Magi as well, though they were a lot closer to what would eventually be called Sorcerers/Hedge Wizards compared to what we got in Mage: The Ascension. There's also Mummy, but that's at the tail end of 1e, IIRC. Minor nitpick but still.<br /> <br /> V5 is street-level and focused on the Cam vs. Anarchs, but that's about it. It's still the &quot;True Art Personal Horror&quot; One True Wayist approach, moreso than any other iteration of Vampire, be it Masquerade or even Requiem. The vast setting changes were also very intense and IMHO, downright god-awful.<br /> <br /> If V5 is &quot;True Art Personal Horror&quot;, Revised is &quot;True Art Personal Horror But With Cataclysmic Gehenna Metaplot Happenings&quot;, 2e is &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas Vampions Badwrongfun&quot;, and V20 is &quot;If You Like Your Style, You Can Play it!&quot;, then 1e is &quot;Trenchcoats &amp; Katanas Vampions Badwrongfun With Bare Minimum Lip Service Paid To Personal Horror&quot;, which IMHO is the best way to approach something like Vampire: The Masquerade. When I ran my VTM one-shots, regardless of edition, I took the 1E mentality.<br /> <br /> It's unironically having your cake and eating it too.<br /> <br /> And yes, you could run any of the editions of Vampire in any style (even V5 theoretically could support any style with HEAVY amounts of homebrewing) but we're talking about what the official books generally espoused and pushed towards.<br /> <br /> TLDR - If V5 is &quot;Street Level Personal Horror&quot;, then V1 is &quot;Street Level Vampions Plus Romanticism&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-27-2024, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T14:24:25-08:00","id":1529568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529565#post1529565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Thematic First Edition&quot;: Alien Hunger, Ashes to Ashes, Blood Bond, Chicago by Night, Diablerie: Mexico, Hunter's Hunted, Milwaukee by Night, Mummy, The Succubus Club<br /> <br /> &quot;Thematic Second Edition&quot;: The Player's Guide to the Sabbat, Children of the Inquisition, the Clan Books, Elysium, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand, Kindred of the East, and so son.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for the double post and double quote, but I'm genuinely curious about something.<br /> <br /> Were <i>Children of the Inquisition </i>and <i>A World of Darkness</i> First Edition or Second Edition books? Both came out in 1992 and while most of the 1992 books for Vampire were 1e, a few of the books in the latter half of 1992 were 2E such as the V2 Corebook, Clanbook Brujah, and The Player's Guide To The Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The reason why I ask is because when I look up those two books in particular, I get mixed messages on whether or not they were 1e or 2e. I don't own either book so I can't say for sure since 1e books have a very distinct look and feel to them. I'm going to assume that A World of Darkness might be one of the last 1e books, given there was a Second Edition version released later on, but Children of the Inquisition seems like it might be one of the first 2e books since it supposedly introduces some characters who'd later become part of the metaplot in late 2e and Revised.<br /> <br /> With the wider Greenberg Era, the Vampire metaplot largely was confined to the Chicago area and this was still mostly true up until the very end of 2e/start of Revised.<br /> <br /> Most of the major metaplot characters introduced in 1e were either only really part of that Chicago metaplot prior to V5, maybe got brief references in later Revised books (like the traveling Succubus Club rave started by Helena) or didn't become major metaplot figures until V5 (Carna and Agent Shepherd probably being the most notable examples)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T15:25:36-08:00","id":1529570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529568#post1529568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"