true up until the very end of 2e/start of Revised.<br /> <br /> Most of the major metaplot characters introduced in 1e were either only really part of that Chicago metaplot prior to V5, maybe got brief references in later Revised books (like the traveling Succubus Club rave started by Helena) or didn't become major metaplot figures until V5 (Carna and Agent Shepherd probably being the most notable examples)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m inclined to agree with you about World of Darkness and Children of the Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T21:54:27-08:00","id":1529581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529572#post1529572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen multiple lists that list the books and half of them list those two books as 1e and the other half as 2e. I'm gonna have to buy those books to see for myself to be sure.<br /> <br /> But overall, I'd agree with you on that. Werewolf getting its own gameline was a massive gamechanger for WoD, especially with its unique cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I view them as transitional books really. They're books that start moving things from local street level play to Elder and international one.<br /> <br /> Just like Under a Blood Red Moon may be a 2nd Edition book but it is designed to transition 1st Edition to 2nd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-28T20:24:10-08:00","id":1529631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529581#post1529581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I view them as transitional books really. They're books that start moving things from local street level play to Elder and international one.<br /> <br /> Just like Under a Blood Red Moon may be a 2nd Edition book but it is designed to transition 1st Edition to 2nd.</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> <br /> Under A Blood Red Moon was also the beginning of the Vampire metaplot too.<br /> <br /> It's saddening to think that from a certain perspective, that book was also the first step on a long arduous road that led to the chaotic base breaker that is V5.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Werewolf probably had more metaplot than Vampire prior to Revised Edition. Most of that concerned Samuel Haight of all things and IIRC, wasn't UABRM a dual Vampire/Werewolf release?<br /> <br /> So, Werewolf was definitely a game changer for the entire WoD in a lot of ways. The metaplot of the entire franchise began there with the Samuel Haight adventure modules, more or less. As much as I love Classic Werewolf, it's sad to know that the concept of a WoD metaplot came from that gameline","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 01-29-2024, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T02:44:13-08:00","id":1529634,"title":"","content":"I would question whether what might be called the Chicago Chronicles (after the reprint series) truly qualify as metaplot. I would argue that metaplot constitutes those events which shape the game world, and justify changes in material gameplay; these are events like the Gangrel leaving the Camarilla, Dementation returning to the Malkavians, the time of thin blood, the decimation of the Ravnos. The events in Chicago really aren't all that. They make a different to chronicles in Chicago, but don't have a significant effect outside the city limits. Effectively, Chicago presents a set of self-contained stories with which characters can interact, but where the consequences do not have a broader impact.<br /> <br /> (It's worth considering why we had <i>Under a Blood Red Moon</i>. So, <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> turned out to be a success, and people wanted to set chronicles in Chicago, which would involve acquiring the already out-of-print <i>Chicago by Night</i>. Reprints are, of course, not a great way to fill up your printing slots in the era before print-on-demand, and White Wolf was faced with a problem, which is that quite a few of the characters in the book were (arguably) the copyright of Upton Sinclair, and used without permission. You could kill them all off, though it might require a fair bit of your word count ... but what about publishing a book so players could experience the cull? And what about throwing a crossover in there on the way? So a bunch of problem characters are killed, a number of other characters also die, White Wolf gets a book which can be sold to storytellers of both <i>Vampire: the Masquerade</i> and <i>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</i>, and the writers get an excuse to write a new edition of <i>Chicago by Night </i>which can be sold to people who already own the first edition, due to the changes. What's not to like?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T11:14:47-08:00","id":1529653,"title":"","content":"I do agree that there is a distinction between what goes on in the Chicago Chronicles and what we generally call metaplot although I do think that there\u2019s also some interesting kernels of overlap or nuance between the two.<br /> <br /> While I can definitely see how one might personally prefer not to run with the events of the Chicago Chronicles as canon for their games and as such might chafe under the suggestion of their having some greater weight in deliberation as \u2018metaplot\u2019 on the other hand I do enjoy some of the narrative threads which run through the old World of Darkness and enjoy playing with them. Now this isn\u2019t to say that old White Wolf necessarily always handled these narrative threads well or wasn\u2019t at times heavy handed with their deployment of them as part of the metaplot, but the golden nuggets there still remain imo.<br /> <br /> This of course is only my personal preference (in fact I usually don\u2019t like to play with the scenario of Under A Blood Red Moon necessarily happening because I feel Lodin is too iconic to ditch that quickly) but I enjoy trying to construct in my head a World of Darkness with a sense of setting verisimilitude where the events in a significant city such as Chicago would have repercussions in other domains (even if it\u2019s just most strongly felt in the North American Midwest). This isn\u2019t to disagree with anything that has been said above by others but more to offer another perspective on the interest of these more grounded narrative threads (as opposed to entirely personal narratives which have relatively little impact outside a few particular individuals or the massive narrative threads which follow antediluvians and metaphysical chicanery and the like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T11:54:17-08:00","id":1529655,"title":"","content":"Like, if I was going to run a classic Chicago Chronicles game using only the official materials (plus a prelude for the PC's) and modules but ignoring Gehenna or any V5 materials, then I'd imagine the whole thing would look like this...<br /> <br /> <br /> ACT I - Forged In Steel<br /> <br /> Prelude<br /> Blood at Dawn<br /> Baptism By Fire<br /> <br /> ACT II - Chicago By Night <br /> <br /> Ashes to Ashes<br /> The Succubus Club<br /> Blood Bond<br /> <br /> ACT III - The War of Chicago<br /> <br /> Awakening: Diablerie Mexico<br /> Milwaukee By Night<br /> Under A Blood Red Moon<br /> <br /> <br /> EPILOGUE<br /> <br /> Dust to Dust<br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC, Chicago By Night 2e didn't come with a pre-made adventure like Milwaukee By Night did (I know for a fact that Chicago By Night 1e doesn't) <br /> <br /> Awakening: Diablerie Mexico isn't officially part of the Chicago Chronicles but it's mentioned how it can be incorporated into a Chicago By Night chronicle, so I'll include it as a part of Act III since Lupines are present in it and that can act as a thematic tie-in for the other two works listed in this third act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T12:36:32-08:00","id":1529660,"title":"","content":"If I was going to be involved in a Chicago setting it would having something to do with Brownyn and paying off a boon that my player character might have with her and having something to do with Newman and the Nosferatu neonate Wanaka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T13:07:25-08:00","id":1529661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529660#post1529660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was going to be involved in a Chicago setting it would having something to do with Brownyn and paying off a boon that my player character might have with her and having something to do with Newman and the Nosferatu neonate Wanaka.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 5th Edition Chicago is quite good but this is based on 1st Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T14:30:01-08:00","id":1529666,"title":"","content":"Bit of an unrelated note, but are WoD materials from White Wolf Magazine eligible for use in the Storyteller's Vault?<br /> <br /> Asking because I think it'd be really cool to do an STV supplement for 1E VTM featuring the characters and other elements from the &quot;Purgatory&quot; article from White Wolf Magazine Issue 28 (which I own a copy of, alongside the fabled Issue 26 that had the preview packet for VTM 1e)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-29T21:38:09-08:00","id":1529689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529458-1st-edition-classic-vampire-reimagining-forged-in-steel?p=1529666#post1529666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of an unrelated note, but are WoD materials from White Wolf Magazine eligible for use in the Storyteller's Vault?<br /> <br /> Asking because I think it'd be really cool to do an STV supplement for 1E VTM featuring the characters and other elements from the &quot;Purgatory&quot; article from White Wolf Magazine Issue 28 (which I own a copy of, alongside the fabled Issue 26 that had the preview packet for VTM 1e)</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, yes. White Wolf Magazine was owned by White Wolf, so should fall under the character usage guidelines for the Storytellers Vault (\u201cAny character published by World of Darkness is available for use.\u201d is the specific wording. If you want to double check, though, you can ask the question in the copyright section of the World of Darkness Discord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}